<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Israel's defense minister has ordered every crossing over the Litani River in south Lebanon destroyed.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Demolishing those bridges will cut the south off from the rest of the country, trapping more than one million people already displaced by the war with no route to safety... no access to hospitals, no path to the north.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Lebanese officials warned Sunday that a ground invasion is now imminent.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iran's military command has threatened to destroy the desalination plants that supply drinking water to millions across the Gulf.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The warning from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈkɑːtəm æl ænˈbiːjɑː">Khatam Al-Anbiya</phoneme> came as US airstrikes continue hitting Iranian power infrastructure, and Trump's forty-eight-hour ultimatum on the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> approaches its deadline.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Countries like Bahrain, Kuwait, and the UAE depend almost entirely on desalinated seawater — if those plants go dark, a humanitarian crisis would unfold within days.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Washington is planning its largest war spending package since Iraq.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth wants two hundred billion dollars for what he called "what we may have to do in the future," while Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent insists the US has plenty of money for Iran.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Neither official has submitted a formal appropriations request — Congress hasn't been asked to authorize a single dollar.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A US Patriot missile — not an Iranian drone — likely struck civilians in Bahrain on March ninth.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Bahrain and US Central Command initially blamed an Iranian drone for thirty-two civilian injuries, until Reuters published an analysis by academic researchers identifying a US-operated Patriot battery on Sitra island as the probable source.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Neither the Pentagon nor Bahrain's government has acknowledged the finding, and no investigation has been announced.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cuba's power grid has collapsed for the third time this month.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>A US oil blockade — now three months old — has strangled supply to a country that generates just forty percent of its own fuel, and the island's eleven million people are living through rolling blackouts with no end in sight.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Havana's deputy foreign minister warned Sunday that Cuba is now preparing for a US military attack.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli settlers burned homes across four Palestinian villages in the West Bank on Saturday.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Settler violence has surged since the US and Israel attacked Iran — six Palestinians killed by settlers since March first, according to the United Nations, a pace not seen since the second intifada.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Israeli police say they're investigating one of the killings; the other five remain unaddressed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russian recruiters tricked two hundred and fifty-two Kenyans into fighting in Ukraine by promising them civilian work.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The men signed Russian-language military contracts they couldn't read, and were deployed directly to the front — a recruitment pipeline that exploited economic desperation in East Africa.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Kenya's secured amnesty for those who return, but a hundred and sixty Kenyans are still trapped on the battlefield.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Runoff voters in France blocked the National Rally in both Toulon and Nîmes.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Marine Le Pen's party led both cities' first rounds but fell when centre-left and centre-right voters formed the familiar barrage — the tactical alliance that's kept the far right from power in French cities for decades.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Former prime minister Édouard Philippe also won Le Havre, positioning himself as the main rival to Le Pen's movement ahead of next year's presidential race.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kim Jong Un's close aide Jo Yong-won now chairs North Korea's parliament.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The Supreme People's Assembly always convenes after a party congress to rubber-stamp its decisions into law — a ritual that keeps both bodies firmly under Kim's inner circle.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The session's happening while global attention is consumed by the Iran war, which is precisely when Pyongyang prefers to move.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's government tripled the premium fuel levy to three hundred rupees per litre and banned spectators from its premier cricket league — all under austerity rules triggered by Iran's closure of the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme>.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The strategy targets luxury consumption to shield ordinary drivers: high-octane fuel absorbs the surcharge while standard petrol prices hold, saving nine billion rupees a month.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The country's also imposed a four-day work week — the kind of peacetime measure no one imagined a month ago.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Niger declared Africa's largest gas pipeline imminent on Sunday.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The four-thousand-kilometre Trans-Saharan route would carry thirty billion cubic metres of Nigerian gas to Europe — a project frozen since Niger's twenty twenty-three coup severed ties with Algeria.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Algeria's state energy company Sonatrach surveyed the route this month, and construction could begin within a year, God willing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Australia's own fuel agency predicted a seventy-five percent shortage last May — and the government did nothing for ten months.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The classified report, obtained under freedom-of-information laws, warned of severe damage to agriculture and logistics, the kind of structural failure that takes years to repair.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Regional towns are already running dry, and Canberra is now scrambling to manage a crisis it was explicitly warned about.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>An enslaved woman's prayer to Venus has survived nearly two thousand years beneath Pompeii's volcanic ash.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The Ancient Graffiti Project, led by historian Rebecca Benefiel, recovered her words — along with thousands of other inscriptions that an eighteen-forties German archaeologist dismissed as trivial, halting an entire field of study for a century.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The project's now catalogued over eight hundred thousand inscriptions, rewriting Roman social history from the voices of people that scholars chose to forget.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Britain's Financial Conduct Authority has handed Palantir access to its fraud and money-laundering intelligence.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The firm — co-founded by Peter Thiel, a major donor to President Trump — already holds five hundred million pounds in UK public contracts spanning the NHS, military, and police.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>A three-month trial will determine whether a single US company gets permanent access to the financial surveillance data of an entire nation.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A developer's rebuilt the nineteen ninety-six 3dfx Voodoo graphics chip entirely in code.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The project replicates in open-source hardware description language what once required a full corporate engineering team — and it runs on a field-programmable gate array you can buy for under a hundred dollars.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The code's on GitHub as a template, meaning other extinct chips from the nineties could now be brought back from the dead.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Most JavaScript frameworks still ship code written for Internet Explorer six — a browser Microsoft killed over a decade ago.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The legacy persists because npm dependency trees carry ancient polyfills as defaults, and the developers who download them have no idea they're included.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Framework maintainers must actively decide to drop dead-browser support — a decision most have quietly avoided for years.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>